ks</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/willmacaskill/status/1968759901620146427</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/willmacaskill/status/1968759901620146427</guid><pubDate>Sat, 20 Sep 2025 15:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[related comments from Seb Krier]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/G1JptQIWEAAj0li.jpg:large"></p><p>Séb Krier (@sebkrier) on X</p><p>I think our entire ontology for how we talk about and conceptualise A[G]I is confused. And I wouldn’t be surprised if in ten years we will look back at the discourse today and laugh at how primitive some ideas are. A few hot and uncertain takes: The way people talk about future</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/sebkrier/status/1968753358216302894">https://x.com/sebkrier/status/1968753358216302894</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/saturday-assorted-links-528.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-528">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/sebkrier/status/1968753358216302894</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/sebkrier/status/1968753358216302894</guid><pubDate>Sat, 20 Sep 2025 15:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[yes way out of date]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://asteriskmag.com/issues/11/iabied">https://asteriskmag.com/issues/11/iabied</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/saturday-assorted-links-528.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-528">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://asteriskmag.com/issues/11/iabied</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://asteriskmag.com/issues/11/iabied</guid><pubDate>Sat, 20 Sep 2025 15:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Agustin sums it up]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1118270039742767105/